<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Monday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	    TONNES	QUALITY	U.S. DOLLAR</p>
<p>PRICE/TONNE</p>
<p> Cameroon		70	   FF	     $1,560</p>
<p> Cameroon	     100	   GF	     $1,684</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   94	   FF	     $1,588</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  100	   FF	     $1,588</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   25	   GF	     $1,642</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  926	   GF	     $1,690 - 1,701</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	1,797	   FF	     $1,598</p>
<p> Ghana		   86	   GF	     $1,712</p>
<p> Ghana		  397	   GF	     $1,715</p>
<p> Ghana		  250	   FF	     $1,683</p>
<p> Malaysia		49	   GF	     $1,548</p>
<p> Nigeria		 82	   FF	     $1,710</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  172	  FAQ	     $1,430</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  101	  FAQ	     $1,430</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ=fair to average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon,  London Newsroom 044 71 542 7928.</p>
